          {
            "_key": "t208n",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "The most common small-business picture: hundreds of impressions, zero clicks. It means Google already considers you an answer — but shows you on page 2–4, where nobody scrolls. That's not a verdict; it's the cheapest growth point there is: content and authority lift what already \"almost works\". It's worse when there are no impressions at all — then the page for that query simply doesn't exist."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
